Video of Panel Mount BulkheadsWhat is a panel-mount bulkhead?Panel mount bulkheads are 
formed by an elongated S-shaped cross-section and an axial passage 
extending from top to bottom. The Panel mount bulkheads are joined by 
tenon in mortise joints, preferably via a spade-shaped tenon. The 
assembly is capped with a channel to position and strengthen the upper 
ends of the panels. A stake positioned through the passage and into the 
earth also secures the panels. The panels are positioned by water flow 
through the passage during the sinking process. Soil stabilization 
chemicals can also be introduced through the passage. A nozzle for the 
lower end of the passage is also disclosed. Panel mount bulkheads are 
made of medical-grade polypropylene and comprise two pieces of fittings,
 the main bulkhead part, and the fixing pieces.What are panel mount bulkheads used for?Panel
 mount bulkheads are used to mount RF connectors and waveguide pipe 
penetrations which cause less impact on the shielding performance. RUNZE
 FLUID produces barbed panel mount bulkheads mainly in natural PP 
material in multiple sizes. RUNZE FLUID is dedicated to manufacturing 
bulkhead connector panels of almost any size. For situations where 
complex hole layouts or connector positions are critical, RUNZE FLUID 
can use precise processing tools to process punch patterns to perfectly 
meet customer requirements.Barbed Panel Mount Bulkheads Features* Barbed bulkhead union for hose connection * Anti-slip and catch-edge design for no leakage 
* Imported raw material, non-toxic, tasteless, heat and corrosion resistant.* PP material is widely used in biomedical, environmental protection and 
